 how many terms are there here I think we should do the sum of the first  $n-2$  terms? 

Answer: We have: 
 \begin{equation*}
\sum_{k=1}^nk = 1+ \cdots + (i-1)+i+(i+1)+\cdots+(j-1)+j+(j+1)+\cdots +n = \frac{n(n+1)}{2}
\end{equation*} 
